      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bobbertoriley/{size}/1910_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-09-28T17:28:08.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Yeah, that's what I was thinking. Another example is, say, Final Wasteland removes a target from a deck before the hero is incapped (example: Final Wasteland removes Mr. Chomps, Unity is incapped, and then is brought back by Rites of Revival. Does Unity come back with a 39 card deck or 40? Seems like a weird set up, but OblivAeon having two environments makes this possible.)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks for checking with Christopher, MigrantP! Out of curiosity, is the Setback situation above (i.e. returning with his tokens) intended behavior or a possible bug?</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:08:02.277Z",
